{"adr":"Decision: choose option A, a responsive web app delivered as wired screen slices.\nThe scaffold owns page structure and component styling; containers add validation, API data, and interactions.\nBoth repos use the shared OpenAPI contract and the web app uses only its generated lib/api client.\nAPI-side persistence, calculations, synchronization, and authorization enforcement remain outside this web implementation.","chosen":"A","complexity":"L","header":{"createdAt":"2026-10-14T16:10:57.918Z","inputsHash":"","kind":"plan","producedBy":{"model":"gpt-6-luna","stage":"plan"},"runId":"20261014-hackathon-problem-statement-fe-95ff","schemaVersion":1},"newDependencies":[],"options":[{"id":"A","simplest":true,"summary":"Implement one wired API-backed slice per approved screen, with shared app foundation first and the API contract generated separately for both repos.","tradeoffs":"Keeps each screen testable as soon as its task lands and avoids a large cross-screen UI layer; requires careful coordination around the shared contract and API client generation."},{"id":"B","simplest":false,"summary":"Build shared data/service layers for all features first, then wire the screens in a later integration task.","tradeoffs":"May centralize repeated logic, but delays screen-level acceptance until integration and creates broad dependencies and overlapping ownership."}],"protectedPathsDeclared":["package.json"],"stubs":[{"content":"export default function SignInContainer() {\n  throw new Error(\"not implemented\");\n}\n","path":"components/screens/s-1/container.tsx","reason":"Public screen container imported by the generated sign-in page and exercised by UI tests."},{"content":"export default function OverviewContainer() {\n  throw new Error(\"not implemented\");\n}\n","path":"components/screens/s-2/container.tsx","reason":"Public screen container imported by the generated overview page and exercised by UI tests."},{"content":"export default function LotsContainer() {\n  throw ne